  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BT CIRT &amp; Policy and Regulatory Issues in the Telecom Sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The task will have three components:  Component 1 : Build capacity and project team for implementation of Computer Incidence Response Team ( CIRT). This component will have six activities described below: The Bank will support and build capacity in the project team to undertake the following five key activities:    (a) Activity I: Create and approve user requirement specification (URS)   (b) Activity II: Design CIRT according to URS.    (c) Activity III: Design network according to URS.    (d) Activity IV: Pre-installation &amp; preparation step by step guide for network and hardware.    (e) Activity V: Remote installation and testing   (f)  Activity VI: Fine tuning of CIRT application &amp; training Of the above six activities, the first three will be conducted simultaneously and will lead to the development of a Consultation Paper for discussion with stakeholders in order to arrive at a set of revised key policies. In the process, DITT will build capacity to conduct public consultation on key policy issues. Component 2: Capacity building on various telecom sector policy issues of DITT Component 3: Capacity building of BICMA on various regulatory issues</narrative>
  </description>
